    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hii, yet another question : )\r\n\r\nLet's say I have a cli process that start from `builtin.cli`, and it took a long time to process, if I tried to stop the picker, the process would still be running in the background.\r\n\r\nThis is not ideal, as I might open file picker on my home directory that `fd` took too long to process, and I would like to cancel it. But now the process will still be running in the background and consume my cpu resources.\r\n\r\nPerhaps not using `builtin.cli` and handle the process creation and call `start()` myself?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hii, yet another question : )</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Let's say I have a cli process that start from <code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.cli</code>, and it took a long time to process, if I tried to stop the picker, the process would still be running in the background.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is not ideal, as I might open file picker on my home directory that <code class=\"notranslate\">fd</code> took too long to process, and I would like to cancel it. But now the process will still be running in the background and consume my cpu resources.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Perhaps not using <code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.cli</code> and handle the process creation and call <code class=\"notranslate\">start()</code> myself?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hii, yet another question : )\nLet's say I have a cli process that start from builtin.cli, and it took a long time to process, if I tried to stop the picker, the process would still be running in the background.\nThis is not ideal, as I might open file picker on my home directory that fd took too long to process, and I would like to cancel it. But now the process will still be running in the background and consume my cpu resources.\nPerhaps not using builtin.cli and handle the process creation and call start() myself?",
