            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Stopping picker on latest `main` branch now also kills the process if it is still running. It means not only with `<C-c>`, but also any \"regular\" way to stop the picker (like `<Esc>`). Tested both with `builtin.files()` and `cli()` with `echo 20` command; both seem to work.\r\n\r\n@jamestansx, thanks for the observation and suggestion!",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Stopping picker on latest <code class=\"notranslate\">main</code> branch now also kills the process if it is still running. It means not only with <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-c&gt;</code>, but also any \"regular\" way to stop the picker (like <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;Esc&gt;</code>). Tested both with <code class=\"notranslate\">builtin.files()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">cli()</code> with <code class=\"notranslate\">echo 20</code> command; both seem to work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/jamestansx/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/jamestansx\">@jamestansx</a>, thanks for the observation and suggestion!</p>",
            "bodyText": "Stopping picker on latest main branch now also kills the process if it is still running. It means not only with <C-c>, but also any \"regular\" way to stop the picker (like <Esc>). Tested both with builtin.files() and cli() with echo 20 command; both seem to work.\n@jamestansx, thanks for the observation and suggestion!",
